B.IT=new A.a8("Musculoskeletal: Spine 5",B.TI)
B.QJ=s(["60 flexion, 50 extension","80 flexion, 70 extension","90 flexion, 90 extension","70 flexion, 80 extension"],t.s)
B.aaJ=new A.e("What are the normal ranges of motion for wrist flexion and extension?",B.QJ,1,"Normal wrist flexion is approximately 80 degrees and extension is 70 degrees. There is slightly more flexion range than extension.")
B.WE=s(["Compartment 3; EPL","Compartment 1; APL and EPB (abductor pollicis longus and extensor pollicis brevis)","Compartment 4; EDC and EIP","Compartment 6; ECU"],t.s)
B.abu=new A.e("Which extensor compartment is the site of De Quervain's tenosynovitis, and what tendons does it contain?",B.WE,1,"De Quervain's involves the first extensor compartment containing the APL and EPB. Finkelstein's test (thumb tucked in fist with ulnar deviation) reproduces pain by stretching these tendons over the radial styloid.")
B.Or=s(["It has dual blood supply that can cause excessive bleeding","Blood enters distally and flows retrograde, so proximal fractures cut off blood supply causing avascular necrosis","It has no direct blood supply","Blood enters proximally and flows distally"],t.s)
B.acK=new A.e("Why is the scaphoid fracture particularly dangerous regarding its blood supply?",B.Or,1,"The scaphoid's blood supply enters at the distal one-third and flows retrograde (backwards) to the proximal pole. A fracture at the waist or proximal pole cuts off blood supply to the proximal fragment, causing avascular necrosis.")
B.MM=s(["50% aspiration, 25% surgical","90% aspiration recurrence, 10% surgical recurrence","30% aspiration, 5% surgical","70% aspiration, 30% surgical"],t.s)
B.aaQ=new A.e("What is the aspiration recurrence rate for ganglion cysts versus surgical excision?",B.MM,1,"Aspiration has a 90% recurrence rate because it drains fluid but does not remove the stalk or valve mechanism. Surgical excision has only a 10% recurrence rate because it removes the entire cyst and stalk.")
B.Pd=s(["Intrinsic muscle contracture pulling the extensor hood","Rupture of the central slip of the extensor tendon allowing the lateral bands to slip volarly, making them act as flexors at the PIP","Volar plate rupture at the DIP joint","Flexor tendon rupture at the MCP joint"],t.s)
B.a67=new A.e("In RA of the hand, what mechanism causes a boutonniere deformity?",B.Pd,1,"Boutonniere deformity occurs when the central slip of the extensor tendon ruptures. The lateral bands migrate volarly (below the axis of rotation) and become flexors at the PIP. The knuckle pops through like a button through a buttonhole (French: boutonniere).")
B.NM=s([B.aaJ,B.abu,B.acK,B.aaQ,B.a67],t.b)
B.IU=new A.a8("Musculoskeletal: Wrist",B.NM)
B.Sw=s(["Level 5 - Supervision","Level 6 - Modified Independence","Level 7 - Complete Independence","Level 4 - Minimal Assist"],t.s)
B.a3Y=new A.e("On the Functional Independence Measure, what is the minimum level at which no physical helper is required?",B.Sw,1,"Level 6 (Modified Independence) and Level 7 (Complete Independence) both require no helper to be physically present. Level 6 allows use of a device or extra time.")
B.XX=s(["Level 2 - Maximal Assist","Level 1 - Total Assist","Level 3 - Moderate Assist","Level 4 - Minimal Assist"],t.s)
B.a6F=new A.e("On the FIM scale, a task that requires two helpers is automatically scored as which level?",B.XX,1,"If a task requires two helpers for any reason, it is automatically scored as Level 1 (Total Assist) regardless of how much effort the patient contributes.")
B.V2=s(["Greater than 10 mmHg","Greater than 15 mmHg","Greater than 20 mmHg","Greater than 25 mmHg"],t.s)
B.aaT=new A.e("What is the ICP threshold at which treatment intervention is required?",B.V2,2,"The threshold for ICP intervention is greater than 20 mmHg. If ICP stays above 20 for more than five minutes, action must be taken.")
B.Vl=s(["Greater than 40 mmHg","Greater than 50 mmHg","Greater than 60 mmHg","Greater than 70 mmHg"],t.s)
B.a8y=new A.e("In the CPP equation (CPP = MAP - ICP), what is the minimum target cerebral perfusion pressure?",B.Vl,2,"The target CPP is greater than 60 mmHg. Data shows that if CPP drops below 50, mortality increases significantly.")
B.Y2=s(["It is cheaper and more widely available","It has a shorter half-life allowing wake-up tests and it lowers ICP","It raises blood pressure which improves cerebral perfusion","It has no significant side effects in TBI patients"],t.s)
B.a6D=new A.e("Why is propofol preferred over benzodiazepines for sedation in the neuro ICU for TBI patients?",B.Y2,1,"Propofol has a very short half-life allowing wake-up tests within minutes, and it also directly lowers ICP. Benzodiazepines have long half-lives that obscure neurological exams.")
B.RD=s([B.a3Y,B.a6F,B.aaT,B.a8y,B.a6D],t.b)
B.IV=new A.a8("Traumatic Brain Injury 3",B.RD)
B.SR=s(["Threshold devices are cheaper","Threshold devices produce resistance independent of flow rate, preventing cheating","Flow-dependent devices are more consistent","Threshold devices are only for COPD"],t.s)
B.a5G=new A.e("What distinguishes a threshold loading device from a flow-dependent device for inspiratory muscle training?",B.SR,1,"Threshold loading requires a predetermined mouth pressure to open a valve regardless of flow rate, so patients cannot cheat by breathing slowly.")
B.Pc=s(["Too noisy for sleep","Negative pressure sucks the upper airway closed, causing severe apnea","Cannot generate enough pressure for obesity","Interferes with CPAP"],t.s)
B.a7t=new A.e("Why is the iron lung contraindicated in obstructive sleep apnea patients?",B.Pc,1,"Negative pressure creates suction that pulls the tongue and soft tissues closed in OSA patients, actively suffocating them each cycle.")
B.WQ=s(["Severe COPD","An inflated cuff","Thick secretions","Age over 80"],t.s)
B.aa8=new A.e("What is the absolute contraindication for a Passy-Muir speaking valve on a tracheostomy patient?",B.WQ,1,"With inflated cuff + one-way valve, air enters but cannot exit \u2014 causing breath stacking, barotrauma, or cardiac arrest.")
B.a_m=s(["100 bpm","110 bpm","120 bpm","140 bpm"],t.s)
B.a9g=new A.e("At what heart rate should exercise be stopped during pulmonary rehabilitation?",B.a_m,2,"If heart rate goes over 120 bpm during pulmonary rehab, hold exercise.")
B.YW=s(["15 degrees","30 degrees","45 degrees","60 degrees"],t.s)
B.a7w=new A.e("What is the minimum angle a patient must be seated at for the pneumobelt to function?",B.YW,1,"The pneumobelt relies on gravity, so the patient must be >30 degrees upright (75 degrees optimal). It cannot work lying flat.")
B.Vy=s([B.a5G,B.a7t,B.aa8,B.a9g,B.a7w],t.b)
B.IW=new A.a8("Pulmonary Rehab 3",B.Vy)
B.TY=s(["It determines the speed of nerve conduction","High skin impedance degrades the recorded signal quality","It calculates the distance between electrodes","It measures the safety factor at the NMJ"],t.s)
B.abO=new A.e("In nerve conduction studies, Ohm's law (I = V/R) is important because:",B.TY,1,"Ohm's law explains that high skin resistance (impedance) reduces the recorded signal. Proper skin preparation reduces impedance, improving signal-to-noise ratio. This is why skin abrasion is critical before electrode placement.")
B.NR=s(["On the contralateral limb","Between the stimulating and recording electrodes","Directly over the motor point","As far from the nerve as possible"],t.s)
B.a4E=new A.e("The ground electrode in nerve conduction studies should be placed:",B.NR,1,"The ground electrode must be placed between the stimulating and recording electrodes to intercept stimulus artifact. Incorrect placement allows artifact to contaminate the recorded signal.")
B.Xv=s(["Adding G1 and G2 signals together","Subtracting G2 from G1 to cancel common noise","Amplifying only the G1 signal","Filtering out all signals below 100 Hz"],t.s)
B.abh=new A.e("A differential amplifier in the EMG machine works by:",B.Xv,1,"The differential amplifier subtracts G2 from G1 (G1 - G2), canceling common-mode noise (60 Hz interference, etc.) while preserving the biological signal. The common mode rejection ratio (CMRR) must be >90 dB.")
B.ZX=s(["20 Hz to 2 kHz","2 Hz to 10 kHz","20 Hz to 10 kHz","1 Hz to 5 kHz"],t.s)
B.abr=new A.e("The standard low-frequency filter (LFF) and high-frequency filter (HFF) settings for motor NCS are:",B.ZX,1,"Motor NCS standard filters: LFF = 2 Hz, HFF = 10 kHz. Sensory NCS uses LFF = 20 Hz, HFF = 10 kHz. Raising the LFF artificially reduces CMAP amplitude; lowering the HFF artificially prolongs latency.")
B.MJ=s(["5% above","10% above","20% above","50% above"],t.s)
B.a9N=new A.e("Supramaximal stimulation in NCS means stimulating at what intensity above the level that produces maximal response?",B.MJ,2,"Supramaximal stimulation is 20% above the intensity that produces the maximal CMAP. This ensures all axons are activated and the response is reproducible. Submaximal stimulation underestimates amplitude.")
