B.Xb=s(["10-20%","30-40%","50-80%","90-100%"],t.s)
B.abY=new A.e("Post-stroke shoulder pain occurs in approximately what percentage of hemiplegic patients?",B.Xb,2,"Hemiplegic shoulder pain is extremely common, occurring in approximately 50-80% of stroke patients. It is one of the most significant barriers to rehabilitation progress and has multiple contributing factors.")
B.a_4=s(["Aggressive passive range of motion","Proper positioning and support of the affected arm","Corticosteroid injection","Surgical repair"],t.s)
B.a6m=new A.e("Which of the following is the most important initial intervention to prevent hemiplegic shoulder subluxation?",B.a_4,1,"Proper positioning and arm support (using arm troughs, lap boards, or slings when upright) is the most important initial intervention. Aggressive passive ROM, particularly overhead pulleys, should be avoided as they can worsen impingement and pain.")
B.T7=s(["First-line therapy for shoulder subluxation","Beneficial for increasing ROM","Contraindicated due to risk of impingement and pain","Only appropriate for flaccid stage"],t.s)
B.a9o=new A.e("Overhead pulleys for hemiplegic shoulder rehabilitation are generally considered:",B.T7,2,"Overhead pulleys are generally contraindicated in hemiplegic shoulders. They can cause impingement, rotator cuff injury, and worsen pain because the patient cannot control the affected arm during the motion.")
B.Ps=s(["Flaccidity with no voluntary movement","Spasticity appears, synergy patterns emerge","Spasticity peaks, voluntary synergy patterns","Spasticity decreases, isolated movements emerge"],t.s)
B.acB=new A.e("Brunnstrom stages of motor recovery describe the progression from flaccidity through spasticity to voluntary movement. What does Stage 3 represent?",B.Ps,2,"Brunnstrom Stage 3 is characterized by peak spasticity and the ability to voluntarily initiate synergy patterns. Stage 1 = flaccidity, Stage 2 = spasticity begins, Stage 3 = spasticity peaks with voluntary synergies, Stage 4 = spasticity decreases with some isolated movement.")
B.a_a=s(["NSAIDs","Opioids","Anticonvulsants or tricyclic antidepressants","Muscle relaxants"],t.s)
B.a9z=new A.e("Central post-stroke pain (thalamic pain syndrome) is best treated initially with which class of medications?",B.a_a,2,"Central post-stroke pain (Dejerine-Roussy syndrome) is a neuropathic pain condition best treated with anticonvulsants (gabapentin, pregabalin) or tricyclic antidepressants (amitriptyline). It does not respond well to NSAIDs or opioids.")
