B.JM=new A.a8("Musculoskeletal: Spine 3",B.a_b)
B.Wk=s(["The kidneys are spared","The lungs are spared","The skin is spared","The brain is spared"],t.s)
B.a9J=new A.e("What is the critical organ-sparing feature that distinguishes polyarteritis nodosa (PAN) from most other vasculitides?",B.Wk,1,"In PAN, the lungs are spared. This is the great differentiator because almost every other vasculitis (Wegener's, Churg-Strauss, Goodpasture's) aggressively attacks the lungs. Clear lungs on a vasculitis vignette points to PAN.")
B.R5=s(["Butterfly rash","Saddle nose deformity","Heliotrope rash","Gottron papules"],t.s)
B.abx=new A.e("What visual buzzword is pathognomonic for granulomatosis with polyangiitis (Wegener's)?",B.R5,1,"The saddle nose deformity results from granulomatous inflammation destroying the nasal septal cartilage, causing the bridge of the nose to collapse inward. It is virtually pathognomonic for Wegener's.")
B.T4=s(["C-ANCA positivity and renal involvement","History of severe asthma and profound eosinophilia","Saddle nose deformity and lung nodules","Hepatitis B association and spared lungs"],t.s)
B.aae=new A.e("What distinguishes Churg-Strauss syndrome (eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis) from other ANCA-associated vasculitides?",B.T4,1,"Churg-Strauss is distinguished by a significant history of asthma (often severe and adult-onset) combined with profound peripheral eosinophilia. It is P-ANCA associated.")
B.Ys=s(["Saddle nose and lung cavitations","Recurrent painful oral and genital ulcers with venous thrombosis risk","Dry eyes and dry mouth","Proximal muscle weakness and heliotrope rash"],t.s)
B.a9u=new A.e("What are the hallmark clinical features of Behcet syndrome?",B.Ys,1,"Behcet syndrome is characterized by recurrent painful oral aphthous ulcers and genital ulcers. About 20% of patients also experience venous thrombosis, distinguishing it from other vasculitides that cause bleeding.")
B.PZ=s(["Distal joint pain with normal ESR","Proximal girdle pain with difficulty abducting shoulders above 90 degrees and ESR greater than 50","Symmetric small joint swelling with positive RF","Muscle weakness with elevated CK"],t.s)
B.a4j=new A.e("In polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR), what is the classic presentation and expected lab finding?",B.PZ,1,"PMR presents with abrupt-onset proximal muscle pain (shoulders and hips), inability to abduct shoulders past 90 degrees, and markedly elevated ESR (>50, often >100). It responds dramatically to low-dose steroids.")
