B.JN=new A.a8("Rheumatology 5",B.Qa)
B.Wl=s(["Resisted external rotation at 0\xb0 abduction","Passive forward flexion with the scapula stabilized","Resisted abduction in the empty can position","Cross-body adduction"],t.s)
B.aac=new A.e("Neer's impingement test involves:",B.Wl,1,"Neer's test: the examiner stabilizes the scapula and passively forward flexes the arm overhead. Pain indicates impingement of the supraspinatus tendon against the anterior acromion.")
B.Qu=s(["Flat","Curved","Hooked","Absent"],t.s)
B.a9c=new A.e("Type III acromion morphology is associated with increased risk of rotator cuff impingement because it is:",B.Qu,2,"Bigliani classification: Type I = flat, Type II = curved, Type III = hooked. The hooked (Type III) acromion narrows the subacromial space, increasing mechanical impingement of the supraspinatus tendon.")
B.Nm=s(["Resisted external rotation at the side","Forward flexing the arm to 90\xb0 then internally rotating","Resisted abduction in the scapular plane","Cross-body adduction with the arm at 90\xb0"],t.s)
B.ad_=new A.e("The Hawkins-Kennedy test for shoulder impingement is performed by:",B.Nm,1,"Hawkins-Kennedy: flex the arm to 90\xb0 then forcefully internally rotate. This drives the supraspinatus tendon against the coracoacromial ligament. Pain = positive for impingement.")
B.Zr=s(["Axillary nerve","Suprascapular nerve","Long thoracic nerve","Dorsal scapular nerve"],t.s)
B.a6K=new A.e("Scapular winging is most commonly caused by injury to which nerve?",B.Zr,2,"The long thoracic nerve innervates the serratus anterior, which holds the scapula against the chest wall. Injury causes medial winging \u2014 the scapula protrudes posteriorly, especially when pushing against a wall.")
B.SZ=s(["Flexion","Abduction","External rotation","Internal rotation"],t.s)
B.a4c=new A.e("Adhesive capsulitis (frozen shoulder) is characterized by loss of both active AND passive ROM. Which motion is typically lost first?",B.SZ,2,"External rotation is typically lost first and most severely in adhesive capsulitis because the inferior glenohumeral ligament (tightest in external rotation) is the first capsular structure to contract. The capsular pattern is external rotation > abduction > internal rotation.")
