B.a5g=new A.e("What is the single worst predictive factor for the inability of sperm to penetrate an ovum in men with SCI?",B.Vr,2,"High concentrations of leukocytes (>10^6) in spermatic fluid is the single worst predictive factor for inability of sperm to penetrate an ovum, reducing count, velocity, and motility.")
B.Rl=s(["Electroejaculation, then PVS, then prostate massage, then surgical extraction","PVS first, then electroejaculation, then prostate massage, then surgical extraction (MESA/TESE)","Prostate massage, then PVS, then electroejaculation, then IVF","Surgical extraction first, then electroejaculation"],t.s)
B.abH=new A.e("What is the correct stepwise algorithm for obtaining sperm from a male SCI patient for fertility purposes?",B.Rl,1,"The algorithm is: (1) penile vibratory stimulation (PVS) as least invasive, (2) electroejaculation if PVS fails, (3) prostate massage, (4) surgical sperm extraction (MESA/TESE) as last resort.")
B.Xz=s(["They interfere with spinal cord healing","The patient is in a hypercoagulable state and estrogen increases clotting risk further","They cause autonomic dysreflexia","They worsen neurogenic bladder"],t.s)
B.a42=new A.e("Why should estrogen-based contraceptives be avoided in the first year after SCI in women?",B.Xz,1,"In the first year post-injury, women are immobilized, have had major trauma, and are in a hypercoagulable state. Adding estrogen, which increases clotting risk, creates a recipe for DVT or PE.")
B.Py=s(["IV magnesium sulfate","Epidural anesthesia extending to T10","General anesthesia","Oral nifedipine"],t.s)
B.a5i=new A.e("During labor in a woman with a T4 SCI, what is the treatment of choice for preventing autonomic dysreflexia?",B.Py,1,"Epidural anesthesia to T10 is used not for pain (she cannot feel contractions) but to block the afferent signal to the spinal cord, preventing the autonomic nervous system from triggering dysreflexia.")
B.So=s(["By urine protein levels only","AD blood pressure is synchronous with uterine contractions (spikes with contractions, drops between them); preeclampsia BP is sustained","AD causes seizures while preeclampsia does not","They cannot be distinguished clinically"],t.s)
B.a9i=new A.e("How can you distinguish autonomic dysreflexia from preeclampsia during labor in a woman with high-level SCI?",B.So,1,"In AD, the high BP is synchronous with contractions - it spikes during contractions and drops back to baseline between them. In preeclampsia, the hypertension is sustained and does not fluctuate with contractions.")
