B.acc=new A.e('The "reading frame hypothesis" explains the difference between Duchenne and Becker muscular dystrophy as:',B.XD,1,"Both affect the dystrophin gene on the X chromosome. Duchenne = out-of-frame deletion producing no functional dystrophin (severe, wheelchair by 12, death by 20s). Becker = in-frame deletion producing shortened but partially functional dystrophin (milder, later onset).")
B.SY=s(["Low amplitude MUAPs","Short duration MUAPs","Polyphasic MUAPs","Decreased recruitment (reduced interference pattern)"],t.s)
B.aaO=new A.e("The classic EMG triad of myopathy includes all EXCEPT:",B.SY,3,"Myopathic EMG triad: low amplitude, short duration, polyphasic MUAPs (sounds like rain on a tin roof). Crucially, recruitment is EARLY \u2014 the brain compensates for weak motor units by recruiting more units sooner. Decreased recruitment is a NEUROPATHIC pattern.")
B.YV=s(["Myasthenia gravis","Duchenne muscular dystrophy","ALS","Guillain-Barr\xe9 syndrome"],t.s)
B.a5M=new A.e("Gower's sign (walking hands up the thighs to stand) is pathognomonic for:",B.YV,1,'Gower\'s sign is pathognomonic for Duchenne MD. The child uses their arms to "climb up" their own legs because proximal hip and thigh muscles are too weak to stand independently. Also characteristic: pseudohypertrophy of calves (fat/fibrosis replacement).')
B.ZM=s(["Proximal weakness only","Distal weakness with multisystem involvement","Pure motor neuron degeneration","Immune-mediated muscle inflammation"],t.s)
B.a6A=new A.e("Myotonic dystrophy (Steinert disease) is unique among myopathies because it causes:",B.ZM,1,"Myotonic dystrophy is distinctive for causing DISTAL weakness (opposite of most myopathies), plus multisystem effects: hatchet face, frontal balding, ptosis, cataracts, cardiac conduction defects, diabetes, testicular atrophy. EMG shows dive-bomber myotonic discharges.")
B.TX=s(["Marching soldiers","Rain on a tin roof","Dive bombers","Machine gun fire"],t.s)
B.a7T=new A.e("The characteristic EMG sound in myotonic dystrophy is described as:",B.TX,2,'Myotonic discharges produce a "dive bomber" sound \u2014 a waxing and waning frequency and amplitude pattern. Myotonia is worsened by cold and improved by warm-up (repeated muscle activation). This auditory pattern is one of the most recognizable EMG findings.')
