B.acH=new A.e("Fibrillation potentials on EMG represent the spontaneous firing of:",B.Yi,1,"Fibrillations are spontaneous discharges of individual denervated muscle fibers. They are not visible through the skin (unlike fasciculations) and produce a high-pitched ticking sound at 20-200 \u03bcV amplitude.")
B.Yw=s(["Benign fasciculations fire at higher rates","Pathologic fasciculations are larger in amplitude","You cannot \u2014 clinical context and the company they keep (fibrillations) are key","Benign fasciculations occur only at rest"],t.s)
B.ad0=new A.e("How can you distinguish benign fasciculations from pathologic fasciculations on EMG?",B.Yw,2,'Fasciculations cannot be reliably differentiated as benign vs pathologic by EMG waveform alone. The "company they keep" principle: fasciculations accompanied by fibrillation potentials and other signs of denervation suggest pathology (ALS, radiculopathy).')
B.MF=s(["Rain on a tin roof","Dive bombers","Marching soldiers","Machine gun fire"],t.s)
B.a9A=new A.e("Myokymic discharges on EMG produce a characteristic sound described as:",B.MF,2,'Myokymia produces a "marching soldiers" sound \u2014 rhythmic grouped bursts of motor unit potentials. It is classically associated with radiation-induced plexopathy and helps distinguish radiation damage from tumor recurrence.')
B.WH=s(["Simple","Biphasic","Triphasic","Polyphasic"],t.s)
B.acE=new A.e("A motor unit action potential (MUAP) with more than 4 phases is described as:",B.WH,3,"Normal MUAPs have 2-4 phases. MUAPs with >4 phases are polyphasic, indicating remodeling of the motor unit \u2014 either from reinnervation (neuropathic) or fiber splitting/regeneration (myopathic). Up to 15% polyphasic MUAPs can be normal.")
B.Vg=s(["The number of fibers near the needle tip","The entire territory (spatial extent) of the motor unit","The conduction velocity of the nerve","The thickness of the myelin sheath"],t.s)
B.ad2=new A.e("MUAP duration on EMG primarily reflects:",B.Vg,1,"MUAP duration represents the entire motor unit territory \u2014 it reflects the timing of all muscle fibers in that motor unit firing. Duration increases in neuropathic conditions (reinnervation creates larger territories) and decreases in myopathies (lost fibers = smaller territory).")
