B.Ry=s(["Transverse myelitis and MS","Spinal stenosis with myelopathy and spinal cord tumors","Epidural abscess and vascular malformation","Syringomyelia and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis"],t.s)
B.aaB=new A.e("What are the two most common causes of non-traumatic spinal cord injury seen in inpatient rehab centers?",B.Ry,1,"Spinal stenosis with myelopathy and spinal cord tumors are the most common non-traumatic causes of SCI seen in inpatient rehab.")
B.Ql=s(["Half recover, half do not","Rule of thirds: one-third recover fully, one-third no improvement, one-third partial recovery","Most patients recover completely within 6 months","90% have permanent severe deficits"],t.s)
B.acD=new A.e("What is the prognosis rule for transverse myelitis?",B.Ql,1,"The rule of thirds states: one-third recover completely, one-third show no improvement with severe permanent deficits, and one-third have partial recovery with significant residual issues.")
B.Oj=s(["Short lesions less than one segment","Longitudinally extensive transverse myelitis spanning more than three vertebral segments","Peripheral ring-enhancing lesions","Multiple small ovoid periventricular lesions"],t.s)
B.a9R=new A.e("What is the radiographic hallmark of neuromyelitis optica (NMO) that distinguishes it from MS on MRI?",B.Oj,1,"NMO characteristically shows longitudinally extensive transverse myelitis (LETM) spanning more than three vertebral segments, unlike MS which typically has short lesions of fewer than two segments.")
B.T5=s(["Hand weakness","Bladder dysfunction","Gait disturbance","Neck pain"],t.s)
B.aap=new A.e("In cervical spondylotic myelopathy, what is usually the very first clinical sign?",B.T5,2,"Gait disturbance is almost always the first sign of cervical spondylotic myelopathy, appearing before hand weakness or major bladder issues.")
B.Ri=s(["Spinal cord infarction","Early postoperative dysphagia","CSF leak","Vertebral artery injury"],t.s)
B.a45=new A.e("What specific risk is associated with the anterior surgical approach for cervical spondylotic myelopathy?",B.Ri,1,"The anterior approach carries a higher risk of early postoperative dysphagia because the esophagus and trachea must be retracted to access the spine.")
