B.a4D=new A.e("Which anti-epileptic drug is associated with an ADH-like effect causing hyponatremia?",B.Sq,2,"Carbamazepine has an ADH-like effect that causes the body to retain water, diluting serum sodium and leading to hyponatremia with decreased serum osmolality.")
B.Vu=s(["Serum sodium","Ammonia level","Phenytoin trough level","Serum calcium"],t.s)
B.a44=new A.e("A TBI patient on valproic acid becomes increasingly confused with normal liver enzymes. What lab value should be checked?",B.Vu,1,"Valproic acid can cause hyperammonemia by interfering with the urea cycle, even when liver enzymes are normal. Elevated ammonia can mimic hepatic encephalopathy.")
B.a_8=s(["Gingival hyperplasia","Hirsutism","Cerebellar atrophy","Megaloblastic anemia"],t.s)
B.aby=new A.e("Which chronic side effect of phenytoin is particularly devastating from a rehabilitation perspective?",B.a_8,2,"Chronic phenytoin toxicity can cause permanent cerebellar atrophy, directly undermining balance and coordination rehabilitation efforts in TBI patients.")
B.QF=s(["Levetiracetam","Gabapentin","Carbamazepine","Phenobarbital"],t.s)
B.a4A=new A.e("Which anti-epileptic drug is a potent enzyme inducer that can lower levels of phenytoin and valproic acid when added to a regimen?",B.QF,2,"Carbamazepine is a potent cytochrome P450 inducer that accelerates the metabolism of other drugs, lowering levels of phenytoin, valproic acid, and haloperidol.")
B.a_1=s(["Sedation and weight gain","Gingival hyperplasia and hirsutism","Irritability, depression, and suicidality","Paradoxical hyperactivity in children"],t.s)
B.ach=new A.e("What is the behavioral side effect profile most associated with levetiracetam (Keppra)?",B.a_1,2,"Levetiracetam is associated with irritability, depression, and even suicidality, sometimes called Keppra rage, which can be difficult to distinguish from TBI-related behavioral changes.")
