B.a5c=new A.e("To confirm a radiculopathy on EMG, abnormalities should be found in at least:",B.Ux,1,'The "two-muscle, two-nerve, one-root rule": abnormalities must be found in at least 2 muscles innervated by different peripheral nerves but sharing the same nerve root. This pattern excludes a single peripheral nerve lesion.')
B.P1=s(["Day 1-2","Day 4-5","Week 1 (day 7)","Week 3-4"],t.s)
B.a7j=new A.e("In radiculopathy, fibrillation potentials first appear in the paraspinal muscles at approximately:",B.P1,2,"Radiculopathy chronology: Day 0 = decreased recruitment only. Day 4-5 = CMAP amplitude drops. Week 1 = fibrillations in paraspinals first (shortest axons from root). Weeks 2-3 = fibrillations appear in limb muscles. Week 5-6 = early reinnervation potentials.")
B.MO=s(["Absent","Low amplitude","Normal (preserved)","Prolonged in latency"],t.s)
B.ac6=new A.e("In radiculopathy, SNAPs are characteristically:",B.MO,2,"SNAPs are NORMAL in radiculopathy because the lesion is pre-ganglionic (proximal to the DRG). The sensory neuron cell body and its peripheral axon remain intact. This is the key finding that distinguishes radiculopathy from plexopathy or peripheral neuropathy.")
B.a_z=s(["Peripheral nerve","Brachial plexus","Nerve root","Spinal cord"],t.s)
B.a5R=new A.e("Abnormal paraspinal muscles on EMG help localize the lesion to the:",B.a_z,2,"Paraspinal muscles are innervated by the posterior rami, which branch off the nerve root before the plexus. Abnormal paraspinals = root-level lesion. Normal paraspinals with limb abnormalities = plexus or peripheral nerve lesion.")
B.U1=s(["Wrist extensors and triceps","Deltoid and biceps (shoulder abduction and elbow flexion)","Hand intrinsics and finger flexors","Forearm pronators and wrist flexors"],t.s)
B.aai=new A.e("The C5 nerve root innervates which key muscles?",B.U1,1,"C5 myotome: deltoid (shoulder abduction) and biceps (elbow flexion). C6 = wrist extension, brachioradialis. C7 = triceps, wrist flexion. C8 = finger flexors. T1 = hand intrinsics. Knowing myotomes is essential for localizing radiculopathies.")
